# finish/etch: T4's etching on P (STYLE_P2 27.3; P2C_CONTRACTS 3b; LADDER-FINISH, ladder slice i3): engraved lines two
# steps under the plane (step-1 lines on step-3 metal), CONNECTED so they read as one cut line: a running wave on a brow
# band (period 4: a chain of lozenges), a lozenge round the boss on a shield, a chevron over the chest gem, a V on a
# pauldron. Never a checker, never dither, never a lone dot. A FIT tile: the view etch<w>x<h> with the largest area
# that fits the part's P box, centred on it (cells off P skipped). K (ink 0) moves the step by -2 on panels; k (ink 1)
# by -1 on brow bands, which are shaded right across (clamped 1..4).
# Generated by LADDER-FINISH's gen_finish.py (keep the drawings there in step).
# (FORGE-MARKS forge i1) the forge styles' panel sizes: Nx1 band lips and vent webs, 1xN / 2xN ribs and flutes, 3x5 3x6 plackart planes, 5x5 6x6 medallions.
# (FORGE-MARKS forge i2) fits for the smallest panels the forge styles leave (1x1, 1x2, 1x3, 2x1: the fluted chest's valley, the plackart seen from the side, a cop's heart), so every style takes its tier finish.
use person
body adult
role overlay finish.etch
legend k ink 1
tags tile overlay fit
on-region P

